  "summary": "Bankura horse  is the terracotta horse, produced in Panchmura village in Bankura district in the Indian state of West Bengal.",
  "description": "Bankura horse  is the terracotta horse, produced in Panchmura village in Bankura district in the Indian state of West Bengal. It has been praised for \"its elegant stance and unique abstraction of basic values.\" Originally used for village rituals, it now adorns drawing rooms around the world as symbols of Indian folk-art. It is the logo of All India Handicrafts.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, West Bengal; registration 2017–18), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
